## Original Content
Investors will buy your life insurance policy today — and collect the payout when you die.

## Summary
The AIDS crisis catalyzed the creation of a multibillion-dollar market where investors purchase life insurance policies from individuals, often those with life-threatening illnesses, and collect the death benefit upon their death. This practice has evolved into a significant financial industry centered on speculation regarding human mortality.

## Key Points
- The AIDS crisis was a pivotal factor in developing the death-speculation market.
- Investors acquire life insurance policies at a discounted rate from policyholders.
- Investors receive the full death benefit when the insured person passes away.
- This market has expanded into a multibillion-dollar financial sector.
- It involves ethical and economic considerations related to speculation on life and death.


